# 0008. Allowlist runtime images and gate remote model code

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-11

Fixes SEC-001: only config decides which container images and which model code may run on
rented GPUs; the API can only choose among approved options.

## Technical details
- **Problem** (SEC-001): a model's `runtime` settings and a deployment's `runtime_config`
  could name any container image, enable `trust_remote_code` or pass any `extra_args`. A
  holder of the management token could run their own code on a RunPod GPU next to `HF_TOKEN`
  and `VLLM_API_KEY`.
- **Config** (`runtime` section):
  - `runtime.image` (default `vllm/vllm-openai:v0.33.0`) is always allowed;
    `runtime.allowed_images` lists any other image a model may name.
  - `runtime.allow_trust_remote_code` (default `false`) gates `trust_remote_code`.
  - `runtime.allow_extra_args` (default `false`) gates free-form `extra_args`.
- **Enforcement** (`adapters/outbound/inference/vllm/vllm.go`, when a deployment is
  prepared): an image not allowed fails with "runtime.image ... is not in
  runtime.allowed_images"; `trust_remote_code` / `extra_args` without their flag fail too.
  Errors are collected and returned together.
- **No flag injection**: string settings and the model artifact may not start with `-`. vLLM
  args are built from typed fields only: `--model`, `--served-model-name`, `--host 0.0.0.0`,
  `--port`, then optional `--max-model-len`, `--dtype`, `--gpu-memory-utilization`,
  `--tensor-parallel-size`, `--quantization`, `--trust-remote-code`, `--enforce-eager`.
  The key goes in the environment (`VLLM_API_KEY`), never in args.
- **Per-model only**: `perModelOnly = image, trust_remote_code, extra_args`: a deployment's
  `runtime_config` can't set them; only the model in the catalog can.
- **Why no deny list**: vLLM has several code-loading flags (`--worker-cls`,
  `--middleware`, ...) and its parser accepts abbreviations and underscores
  (`--trust-remote`, `--trust_remote_code`), so a deny list is bypassable.
- **Consequences**: a leaked management token can no longer run custom containers or remote
  code. A new vLLM image or a model needing remote code needs a config change and restart.

## Technologies and alternatives
- Involved: vLLM OpenAI server image.
- Alternatives: deny-list flags in `extra_args`: bypassable as above; pass `HF_TOKEN` only to
  models that ask: a custom image still runs arbitrary code; models in config only: loses
  the API's model editing.
